VALUES ('CRWV','bear_case','editorial_analysis','CoreWeave reported $25.15 billion of principal debt at March 31, 2026, plus $16.98 billion of undiscounted operating-lease payments. The top two customers generated approximately 65% of Q1 revenue, and customers can also be competitors or build internal infrastructure. All GPUs in CoreWeave’s infrastructure were NVIDIA GPUs because of customer contract requirements, creating concentrated technology and supply dependence. Adjusted operating margin fell to 1% from 17% a year earlier; net interest expense reached $536 million and the quarter produced a $740 million GAAP net loss.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','CoreWeave First-Quarter 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1769628/000176962826000222/crwv-20260331.htm','The filing reports $2.08B of Q1 revenue, a $740M net loss, $25.15B of principal debt, $2.24B of cash, $7.70B of property-and-equipment purchases, 65% revenue concentration among the top two customers, and the company’s material risk disclosures.','2026-05-07','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
