VALUES ('CRWV','thesis_breaker','editorial_analysis','The thesis breaks if capacity delivery slips, customers reduce or reprice commitments, or utilization and cash collections fail to cover debt service, leases, and the replacement cost of rapidly aging accelerators. A large backlog would not protect owners if financing remains structurally more expensive than the returns earned on deployed clusters.','Defines evidence that would invalidate the ownership thesis.','CoreWeave First-Quarter 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1769628/000176962826000222/crwv-20260331.htm','The filing reports $2.08B of Q1 revenue, a $740M net loss, $25.15B of principal debt, $2.24B of cash, $7.70B of property-and-equipment purchases, 65% revenue concentration among the top two customers, and the company’s material risk disclosures.','2026-05-07','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
