VALUES ('DLR','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for global data-center campuses, colocation, interconnection, and digital-infrastructure leasing can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Vacancy, churn, customer consolidation, or property obsolescence can reduce cash flow. Leverage and maturities expose owners to rates and capital-market availability. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','DLR SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001297996&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides DIGITAL REALTY TRUST REIT INC''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
