VALUES ('EQT','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for Appalachian natural-gas production, drilling, gathering coordination, hedging, acreage development, and capital returns can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Prices, spreads, and differentials can reduce earnings and asset values. Incidents, outages, leaks, remediation, or permit restrictions can interrupt cash flow. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','EQT SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0000033213&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides EQT CORP''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
