VALUES ('FCEL','bull_case','editorial_analysis','FuelCell Energy reported a 4 GW Q2 sales pipeline and is packaging its technology in repeatable 12.5 MW blocks aimed at grid-constrained data centers. The company had $1.14 billion of contracted backlog at April 30, 2026, including $928.5 million of long-duration generation backlog and $155.4 million of service backlog. The Siemens collaboration can pair FuelCell Energy''s generation equipment with electrical balance-of-plant design for 100+ MW projects, potentially reducing integration friction for large deployments. ExxonMobil-affiliate work provides a differentiated carbon-capture option: the Rotterdam pilot is intended to test capture technology that can also produce electricity and hydrogen. Unrestricted cash was $373.2 million at April 30, before the July offering generated approximately $225 million of gross proceeds, providing capacity to fund manufacturing and project development.','Preserves the constructive interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','FuelCell Energy Q2 fiscal 2026 results','https://investor.fce.com/press-releases/press-release-details/2026/FuelCell-Energy-Reports-Second-Fiscal-Quarter-2026-Results-Advances-Data-Center-Power-Strategy/default.aspx','The official release reports revenue, gross loss, net loss, adjusted EBITDA, backlog, the 4 GW sales pipeline, manufacturing plans, and business updates.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
