VALUES ('FCEL','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Q2 revenue fell 5% to $35.6 million and gross margin deteriorated to negative 36.3%, including weak generation economics and a Groton-project impairment. The company lost $77.6 million in Q2 and used $61.2 million of operating cash during the first six months of fiscal 2026. Backlog declined 9.9% year over year; product backlog fell to $36.1 million and Advanced Technologies backlog fell to $15.4 million. Fuel costs, module replacements, service guarantees, project availability, and long-lived power-purchase obligations can create losses even after a project begins generating revenue. The July sale of 10.7 million new shares at $21 raised capital but materially expanded the share base; further capacity growth could require additional financing before positive free cash flow is proven.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','FuelCell Energy Q2 fiscal 2026 Form 10-Q','https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/886128/000110465926071183/fcel-20260430x10q.htm','The filing provides segment revenue and cost, backlog composition, project performance, cash flow, cash restrictions, debt, shares outstanding, commitments, and risk factors.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
