VALUES ('FIX','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for mechanical, electrical, plumbing, controls, modular construction, and recurring maintenance services for mission-critical and commercial facilities can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Customer capital spending and large programs can shift abruptly. Materials, skilled labor, supplier performance, warranty, or certification failures can disrupt delivery. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','FIX SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001035983&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides COMFORT SYSTEMS USA INC''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
